      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: why? iiuc, the code below always sets bit 7 (\u0027RMA happened\u0027) to 0. so, if bits 6..0 are not 0b1111111, this bit is already 0. and increment_rma_count(0) in this case is basically NOP. shall we just return success immediately instead of error? that\u0027d allow scripts to call increment_rma_count(0) w/o checking what the current count is first.",
