      "writtenOn": "2018-08-24T03:25:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agree it is safe to always increment by 0; my reasoning for adding this check is that it if you increment by 0 on a device where the count has already been incremented, you leave it in an inconsistent state.\n\nI was imagining a situation like this:\n\n1. increment RMA count by 1: RMA count can be trusted to represent number of RMAs, and map to the current serial number stored server-side  \n\n2. increment RMA count by 0: RMA count appears valid, but does not correspond to actual number of RMAs, or current serial number stored server-side\n\nMy thinking was that if we disallow this pattern, we can always trust the RMA count to be accurate if the values are 1-6.\n\nIf the RMA indicator is set, and the count is either 0 or 7, then we do not know the number of RMAs the device has been through.",
      "parentUuid": "ab074f61_0fc86501",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 123,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "2b32b831df4c93fb71e9294bcdacfcc6ddf0277c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
